-- title:
--   Exit ideal proper iff contained in a maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$, a Weierstrass curve $W$ over $\mathbb{Z}$, and a natural number $p$. Work in the ring $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {n : ℕ | n ∣ N}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the space of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the Hecke operators attached to the excluded set $S = \{n : n \mid N\}$, namely by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ (the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ being excluded by $S$). Let [`ModularCurve.exitIdeal N W p`](def/ModularCurve_SupportTransfer.html#L25) be the ideal of $\mathbb{T}$ spanned by the image of $p$ together with all elements $T_\ell - a_\ell(W)$, where $\ell$ ranges over primes with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \neq p$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$ in $\mathbb{Z}$, and $a_\ell(W)$ is the trace of Frobenius of the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$, cast into $\mathbb{T}$. The assertion is that this ideal is not the whole of $\mathbb{T}$ if and only if there exists a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_1$ of $\mathbb{T}$ containing the image of $p$ and containing $T_\ell - a_\ell(W)$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$ and $\ell \neq p$.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the ideal-theoretic formulation of the exit ideal being proper and the generator-by-generator formulation, namely the existence of a maximal ideal of the anemic integral Hecke algebra of level $N$ at which the system of eigenvalue congruences $T_\ell \equiv a_\ell(W)$ away from $Np\Delta_W$ holds. It feeds [`WeierstrassCurve.isResiduallyModularOfLevel_of_exitIdeal_ne_top`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.isResiduallyModularOfLevel_of_exitIdeal_ne_top), where such a maximal ideal is converted into residual modularity of $W$ at level $N$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exitIdeal_ne_top_iff_exists_maximal.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_SupportTransfer

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem ModularCurve.exitIdeal_ne_top_iff_exists_maximal (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (W : WeierstrassCurve ℤ) (p : ℕ) :
    ModularCurve.exitIdeal N W p ≠ ⊤ ↔
      ∃ 𝔪₁ : Ideal (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {n : ℕ | n ∣ N}), 𝔪₁.IsMaximal ∧
        ((p : ℕ) : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {n : ℕ | n ∣ N}) ∈ 𝔪₁ ∧
        ∀ (ℓ : ℕ) (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) (hℓN : ¬ ℓ ∣ N), W.IsGoodPrimeFor ℓ → ℓ ≠ p →
          ModularCurve.exitGen N W ℓ hℓ hℓN ∈ 𝔪₁ := by sorry
